### Below are notes on how I successfully spun up a vm running little_os:

The following command will run the little_os in a vm:

    qemu-system-i386 -monitor stdio -enable-kvm -m 2048 -nic user,model=virtio -drive file=little_os.qcow2,media=disk,if=virtio -cdrom os.iso

While running the vm, entering the following command in the terminal will show the current state of the registers on the vm:

    info registers

### SOFTWARE VERSIONS USED
Ubuntu 24.04.2 LTS
qemu 8.2.2

